Adjust the locators and avatar URL to your app. **The toast must remain observable long enough for these checks to pass together.** If it disappears before the async update completes, this requirement needs a persistent success indicator or a separate assertion recording the transient toast—not more retries.

## 2. Give each parallel worker a different account

`storageState` isolates browser authentication state, **not server-side user preferences**. Twenty contexts using the same account still overwrite the same language setting.

Use a worker-scoped authenticated state and reset language before each test. This example assumes your app exposes the illustrated login and language endpoints; substitute their real routes/payloads.

```ts
// fixtures.ts
import {
  test as base,
  expect,
  request,
} from '@playwright/test';

type WorkerFixtures = {
  pickerState: Awaited<
    ReturnType<import('@playwright/test').APIRequestContext['storageState']>
  >;
};

export const test = base.extend<{}, WorkerFixtures>({
  pickerState: [
    async ({}, use, workerInfo) => {
      // Must differ across shards AND simultaneous CI runs.
      const poolId = process.env.PICKER_POOL_ID;
      if (!poolId) throw new Error('PICKER_POOL_ID is required');

      const accounts = JSON.parse(
        process.env.PICKER_ACCOUNTS_JSON ?? '{}',
      ) as Record<string, { username: string; password: string }>;

      // parallelIndex stays stable when Playwright replaces a failed worker.
      const key = `${poolId}:${workerInfo.parallelIndex}`;
      const account = accounts[key];
      if (!account) throw new Error(`Missing dedicated picker account: ${key}`);

      const api = await request.newContext({
        baseURL: workerInfo.project.use.baseURL,
      });

      try {
        const login = await api.post('/api/login', { data: account });
        expect(login.ok()).toBeTruthy();
        await use(await api.storageState());
      } finally {
        await api.dispose();
      }
    },
    { scope: 'worker' },
  ],

  storageState: async ({ pickerState }, use) => {
    await use(pickerState);
  },

  // Runs before every test, including tests on a reused worker.
  page: async ({ page }, use) => {
    const response = await page.request.patch('/api/profile', {
      data: { language: 'en' },
    });
    expect(response.ok()).toBeTruthy();

    // Also handles an asynchronous preference update.
    await expect(async () => {
      const profile = await page.request.get('/api/profile');
      expect(profile.ok()).toBeTruthy();
      expect(await profile.json()).toMatchObject({ language: 'en' });
    }).toPass({ timeout: 15_000 });

    await use(page);
  },
});

export { expect };
```

Import that fixture in **all affected specs**:

```ts
import { test, expect } from './fixtures';
```

```ts
// playwright.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  fullyParallel: true,
  workers: 5, // Provision five dedicated accounts per shard/project pool.
  use: {
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:3000',
    // Remove the old shared-picker storageState configuration.
  },
});
```

Provision distinct account pools for concurrent shards, projects, and CI runs. Workers run tests sequentially, so one account per worker plus a per-test reset is sufficient here.

**If only one account exists:** serialize every test that mutates it:

```ts
export default defineConfig({
  fullyParallel: false,
  workers: 1,
});
```

That fallback also requires preventing other shards, projects, or CI runs from using the account concurrently. A serial group in one spec does not serialize other specs.

